From fd08d0f2ddce058c10876703a9fde44f404107e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Giunta <marco_giunta@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:56:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] HID: Add driver for Lenovo Legion Spectrum keyboard
 backlight

Certain Lenovo Legion Gen 10 laptops, such as the Legion Pro 7 16AFR10H,
drive the keyboard backlight with an ITE 8258 USB controller (048d:c197),
which also hosts the internal keyboard.
The firmware's ACPI and WMI keyboard backlight methods are stubs on these
machines, so the backlight is currently not exposed to userspace by the
ideapad-laptop driver.

Add a driver exposing the brightness as the :kbd_backlight LED class
device, using the controller's vendor feature report. The LED offers
"off" plus the three levels used by the firmware's Fn+Up/Down hotkeys
(hardware values 0, 3, 6, 9).
Brightness changes made by the firmware (Fn+Up/Down) are reported through
led_classdev_notify_brightness_hw_changed, using the input report
the controller sends on every state change.

On models where the same controller is used with a single-color backlight,
it answers the driver's compatibility query with 1, and the backlight
remains with ideapad-laptop.

Per-key RGB and effects are left to userspace via hidraw.

The protocol was reverse-engineered by the LenovoLegionToolkit project
(see LenovoLegionToolkit.Lib/Native.cs) [1].

[1] https://github.com/LenovoLegionToolkit-Team/LenovoLegionToolkit

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Marco Giunta <marco_giunta@outlook.it>
